# Build-context excludes. The image is built from this directory, and
# `COPY skills /app/skills` would otherwise pick up whatever a local run left
# behind — notably Python bytecode from the skill scripts under
# skills/*/scripts/. Those are gitignored, so a clean CI checkout never has
# them, but a developer's local build would silently ship them.
#
# NOTE the `**/` prefixes. .dockerignore does NOT use .gitignore semantics: a
# bare `__pycache__/` matches only a directory at the context root, not at any
# depth. Without `**/` these patterns silently match nothing.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
